  {
   "xml_index": 2,
   "xml_name": "PS6_002_Climbing The Stairs",
   "display_name": "Climbing The Stairs",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Imagine Frodo has to climb a staircase of <code>n</code> steps up a mountain. At each move, he can climb <b>1, 2 or 3</b> steps at once. He must land exactly on the top step (he cannot go past it).</p>\n<p>Two ways of climbing are <b>different</b> if the sequence of moves is different, so climbing 1 then 2 is different from climbing 2 then 1.</p>\n<p>For example, a staircase of 3 steps can be climbed in 4 different ways:</p>\n<pre>1 + 1 + 1\n1 + 2\n2 + 1\n3</pre>\n<p>Write a function <code>climb_ways(n)</code> that takes a positive integer (int &gt; 0) <code>n</code>, at most 20, and <b>returns</b> the number of different ways to climb a staircase of <code>n</code> steps.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b> <code>climb_ways(1)</code> returns <code>1</code>. <code>climb_ways(2)</code> returns <code>2</code> (1+1, or 2). <code>climb_ways(3)</code> returns <code>4</code>. <code>climb_ways(4)</code> returns <code>7</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
