  {
   "xml_index": 3,
   "xml_name": "PS6_003_Nested List Sum",
   "display_name": "Nested List Sum",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A <b>nested list</b> is a list whose elements can be integers <b>or other lists</b>, and those inner lists can again contain integers or lists, to any depth. For example:</p>\n<pre>[1, [2, 3], [[4]], 5]</pre>\n<p>Here the elements are: the integer 1, the list [2, 3], the list [[4]] (a list containing the list [4]), and the integer 5.</p>\n<p>Write a function <code>nested_sum(lst)</code> that takes such a nested list and <b>returns</b> the sum of <b>all</b> the integers inside it, at every level. Empty lists (at any level) add 0.</p>\n<p><i>Python fact you may use:</i> <code>type(x) == list</code> is <code>True</code> if <code>x</code> is a list, and <code>False</code> if <code>x</code> is an integer.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>nested_sum([1, [2, 3], [[4]], 5])</code> returns <code>15</code></li>\n<li><code>nested_sum([1, 2, 3])</code> returns <code>6</code></li>\n<li><code>nested_sum([])</code> returns <code>0</code></li>\n<li><code>nested_sum([[[]], [7, [-2]]])</code> returns <code>5</code></li>\n</ul>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(nested_sum([1, [2, 3], [[4]], 5]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "15",
