  {
   "xml_index": 9,
   "xml_name": "PS6_009_Worst Case Guessing Game",
   "display_name": "Worst Case Guessing Game",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Hermione secretly picks an integer between 1 and <code>n</code> (both included). Ron tries to guess it, always using the same strategy:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Ron keeps track of the smallest possible value <code>low</code> (starting at 1) and the largest possible value <code>high</code> (starting at <code>n</code>).</li>\n<li>Ron guesses <code>(low + high) // 2</code>.</li>\n<li>If the guess is correct, the game ends. If Hermione says the secret is <b>larger</b>, Ron sets <code>low</code> to guess + 1. If she says it is <b>smaller</b>, Ron sets <code>high</code> to guess - 1. Then Ron guesses again.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For example, with n = 10 and secret 7: Ron guesses 5 (too small), then 8 (too large), then 6 (too small), then 7 (correct). That game took <b>4</b> guesses, counting the final correct guess.</p>\n<p>How many guesses Ron needs depends on which secret Hermione picked. Write a function <code>max_guesses(n)</code> that takes a positive integer (int &gt; 0) <code>n</code>, at most 500, and <b>returns</b> the <b>largest</b> number of guesses Ron could ever need, over all possible secrets from 1 to <code>n</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b> <code>max_guesses(1)</code> returns <code>1</code>. <code>max_guesses(3)</code> returns <code>2</code> (secret 2 takes 1 guess, secrets 1 and 3 take 2 guesses). <code>max_guesses(10)</code> returns <code>4</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
